1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,200
Oh, here. Looks like it's in exactly two weeks.

2
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:12,480
I mean, what? Two weeks? How am I supposed to build an entire outfit in two weeks?

3
00:00:16,040 --> 00:00:20,220
Is she insane? It already takes me forever to make clothing for Hina dolls.

4
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:24,180
I'm sure it's gonna take at least twice as long to make something for a real live human.

5
00:00:24,180 --> 00:00:31,440
Then again, I've never actually done it before, so I have no frame of reference to even estimate whether it could be possible or not.

6
00:00:33,020 --> 00:00:36,400
This sucks. I have to find a way. I have to.

7
00:00:37,840 --> 00:00:41,820
She's like I was looking forward to this so much. I can't disappoint her.

8
00:00:43,140 --> 00:00:47,520
Anyway, I'll get on it as soon as I'm home. I'll make the patterns first and then start cutting.

9
00:00:48,040 --> 00:00:50,020
Oh, jeez. How long is that gonna take?

10
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:53,760
None of the pieces can be cut in a straight line. They're all curvy.

11
00:00:53,760 --> 00:00:59,360
I'll need at least two or three days. It's no use. There's not enough time.

12
00:00:59,660 --> 00:01:02,820
Uh, there it goes. My mind has been lost.

13
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:06,720
Of course, Slippery Girls could have had something to do with that, too.

14
00:01:06,720 --> 00:01:09,180
Yes, please.

15
00:01:12,180 --> 00:01:13,920
Well, let's help.

16
00:01:20,180 --> 00:01:24,260
What do you think of that is?

17
00:01:24,260 --> 00:01:43,980
Good night.

18
00:01:43,980 --> 00:02:13,960
See you next time.

19
00:02:13,980 --> 00:02:41,540
I'm home.

20
00:02:41,540 --> 00:02:47,180
Oh, good. I was worried. You're, uh, home pretty late today, aren't you?

21
00:02:47,740 --> 00:02:50,980
Um, yeah, I'm sorry. I just got distracted and forgot to call.

22
00:02:51,660 --> 00:02:53,700
It was fun. I went out shopping with a friend.

23
00:02:54,360 --> 00:02:57,260
A friend, huh? That's excellent news, Wakana.

24
00:02:57,700 --> 00:03:02,000
What were you shopping for? Some new books, maybe? Or those little record CDs?

25
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:12,940
Huh? Grandpa, are you okay?

26
00:03:12,940 --> 00:03:21,420
Uh, there you are.

27
00:03:22,540 --> 00:03:25,380
Thanks for coming. It's late. I'm sorry.

28
00:03:26,260 --> 00:03:27,880
Hmm. How's Grandpa?

29
00:03:28,320 --> 00:03:29,920
They're putting a compress on him now.

30
00:03:30,600 --> 00:03:31,100
I see.

31
00:03:31,840 --> 00:03:33,700
Thankfully, it wasn't too bad of a fall.

32
00:03:34,600 --> 00:03:37,300
And that's it. We'll get you something for the pain.

33
00:03:37,420 --> 00:03:38,920
You be careful and watch your step.

34
00:03:39,760 --> 00:03:42,560
Thank you, Doctor. I appreciate all your help.

35
00:03:43,120 --> 00:03:43,520
Grandpa!

36
00:03:44,120 --> 00:03:44,560
Hey!

37
00:03:44,560 --> 00:03:47,460
Don't scare us like that.

38
00:03:47,980 --> 00:03:50,160
What on earth are you doing here, Mayori?

39
00:03:50,280 --> 00:03:51,140
Just take it slow, okay?

40
00:03:51,160 --> 00:03:52,960
Well, I had a blank spot in my schedule.

41
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:55,000
What? I was worried about you.

42
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:59,340
So they want you to stay in bed for two weeks?

43
00:03:59,800 --> 00:04:02,700
Dad suggested that you come stay with us until you're feeling better.

44
00:04:03,300 --> 00:04:04,740
I'm here to bring you home with me.

45
00:04:05,540 --> 00:04:09,000
Yeah, good idea. Plus, their house is closer to the hospital anyway.

46
00:04:09,540 --> 00:04:12,000
We also have a car, in case we need to take you.

47
00:04:12,980 --> 00:04:15,280
All right, then. Just hope I'm not a burden.

48
00:04:15,580 --> 00:04:17,480
Why don't you come spend the night with us tonight?

49
00:04:17,900 --> 00:04:19,180
We've got a futon for you.

50
00:04:19,740 --> 00:04:23,160
Hmm. All right. I'll bring you fresh clothes tomorrow.

51
00:04:23,160 --> 00:04:25,240
Thanks. Sorry about this.

52
00:04:25,820 --> 00:04:27,240
Oh, but...

53
00:04:27,240 --> 00:04:30,060
My brushes. Could you bring them?

54
00:04:35,280 --> 00:04:37,820
Maybe we should take you to an acupuncturist, too.

55
00:04:38,040 --> 00:04:38,540
Sure.

56
00:04:40,020 --> 00:04:41,200
Are you okay?

57
00:04:41,460 --> 00:04:44,280
All this shaking, it's just got me shook up.

58
00:04:44,620 --> 00:04:46,040
No, not okay.

59
00:04:47,420 --> 00:04:48,340
I see.

60
00:04:49,100 --> 00:04:51,200
So that's why you weren't at school yesterday.

61
00:04:51,200 --> 00:04:52,800
Uh-huh.

62
00:04:53,440 --> 00:04:56,640
So, um, I'm going by there again today to check on him.

63
00:04:57,120 --> 00:04:58,600
You must be so worried.

64
00:04:59,600 --> 00:05:02,060
I'd be. Hope he starts feeling better soon.

65
00:05:03,340 --> 00:05:03,820
Yeah.

66
00:05:08,080 --> 00:05:08,860
Hey, Gojo.

67
00:05:09,240 --> 00:05:11,240
Let me know if there's anything I can do to help.

68
00:05:11,660 --> 00:05:14,120
I can't sew, but I can cook and do house stuff.

69
00:05:14,880 --> 00:05:15,880
Thanks, Kitagawa.

70
00:05:15,880 --> 00:05:18,700
But I think I should be fine.

71
00:05:19,100 --> 00:05:20,480
Still, though, it's nice of you.

72
00:05:20,720 --> 00:05:22,380
Right. I get it.

73
00:05:23,160 --> 00:05:25,640
Well, then, let's trade numbers at least.

74
00:05:26,080 --> 00:05:28,380
We ought to have a way to reach each other if something comes up.

75
00:05:28,660 --> 00:05:29,240
Uh, cool?

76
00:05:29,240 --> 00:05:34,200
Yeah, sure.

77
00:05:40,680 --> 00:05:42,100
I'm so far behind.

78
00:05:42,480 --> 00:05:44,880
I didn't work on the outfit yesterday or the day before.

79
00:05:44,880 --> 00:05:47,020
I need to do something today.

80
00:05:47,160 --> 00:05:50,400
By the way, I got the wig cut and it looks super sick.

81
00:05:50,740 --> 00:05:51,620
I brought it to give you.

82
00:05:53,340 --> 00:05:54,360
Hey, are you there?

83
00:05:54,360 --> 00:05:54,600
Huh?

84
00:05:54,840 --> 00:05:55,540
Oh, of course.

85
00:05:55,720 --> 00:05:55,960
Sorry.

86
00:05:57,340 --> 00:05:58,860
Oh, that's right.

87
00:05:58,860 --> 00:06:00,480
My gross midterms are next week.

88
00:06:01,140 --> 00:06:02,720
Could this be more poorly timed?

89
00:06:03,240 --> 00:06:05,460
Especially since I'm the type that needs to cram the night.

90
00:06:05,460 --> 00:06:06,680
No, no, no, no, no, no.

91
00:06:06,900 --> 00:06:07,340
Midterms?

92
00:06:07,920 --> 00:06:08,940
I completely forgot.

93
00:06:09,800 --> 00:06:12,680
Somehow, between visiting Grandpa and studying for tests,

94
00:06:13,140 --> 00:06:15,560
I have to find time to make an entire outfit.

95
00:06:18,560 --> 00:06:19,480
Hey, Gojo.

96
00:06:20,280 --> 00:06:21,160
You okay?

97
00:06:21,300 --> 00:06:21,580
Yes.

98
00:06:22,240 --> 00:06:23,120
Yes, I am.

99
00:06:23,120 --> 00:06:30,400
I think I might be in trouble.

100
00:06:35,780 --> 00:06:36,760
Hello, Gojo dolls.

101
00:06:36,920 --> 00:06:37,580
How can I help you?

102
00:06:38,920 --> 00:06:40,120
You mean a tour of our workshop?

103
00:06:40,440 --> 00:06:41,260
Yes, that's right.

104
00:06:41,400 --> 00:06:44,020
I was told that you offer tours, but if not...

105
00:06:44,020 --> 00:06:44,520
Yes, ma'am.

106
00:06:44,600 --> 00:06:45,120
We sure do.

107
00:06:45,620 --> 00:06:46,560
Oh, that's fantastic.

108
00:06:46,940 --> 00:06:49,120
My friend is very interested in Hina dolls,

109
00:06:49,220 --> 00:06:51,100
so I think he would really enjoy the opportunity.

110
00:06:51,420 --> 00:06:52,880
When are you guys wanting to come in?

111
00:06:52,880 --> 00:06:56,360
Well, um, this is kind of a last-minute request.

112
00:06:56,760 --> 00:06:58,920
We were hoping we could do it May 6th.

113
00:06:59,180 --> 00:06:59,920
That's tomorrow.

114
00:07:00,660 --> 00:07:02,120
Um, I'm terribly sorry.

115
00:07:02,480 --> 00:07:04,160
We're actually closed until next Saturday,

116
00:07:04,720 --> 00:07:07,080
but we can fit you in after that anytime you'd like.

117
00:07:07,280 --> 00:07:08,140
Oh, gosh.

118
00:07:08,240 --> 00:07:09,160
I wish we could,

119
00:07:09,320 --> 00:07:10,260
but you see,

120
00:07:10,400 --> 00:07:12,660
my friend is here visiting all the way from France.

121
00:07:12,980 --> 00:07:15,420
He's actually flying home the day after tomorrow,

122
00:07:15,700 --> 00:07:17,940
so unfortunately that was our only option.

123
00:07:19,260 --> 00:07:20,500
Anyway, sorry to bother you.

124
00:07:20,540 --> 00:07:21,440
I appreciate your help.

125
00:07:21,640 --> 00:07:22,180
No, wait!

126
00:07:22,880 --> 00:07:23,460
We can do it!

127
00:07:23,820 --> 00:07:24,200
Come in!

128
00:07:24,420 --> 00:07:25,400
Oh, really?

129
00:07:25,480 --> 00:07:25,960
You can?

130
00:07:26,200 --> 00:07:27,160
The shop owner's out,

131
00:07:27,260 --> 00:07:28,560
but if you don't mind me doing it,

132
00:07:28,800 --> 00:07:30,500
I can give you a tour after 4.30.

133
00:07:30,660 --> 00:07:31,360
Are you serious?

134
00:07:31,740 --> 00:07:32,440
That's great!

135
00:07:32,520 --> 00:07:33,420
Thank you so much!

136
00:07:34,100 --> 00:07:34,660
Of course.

137
00:07:35,320 --> 00:07:35,680
Okay.

138
00:07:36,360 --> 00:07:36,820
Then, uh,

139
00:07:37,420 --> 00:07:38,280
I'll see you tomorrow.

140
00:07:38,280 --> 00:07:52,540
What have I done?

141
00:07:52,540 --> 00:07:53,400
What's wrong with me?

142
00:07:54,060 --> 00:07:54,760
What do I do?

143
00:07:54,760 --> 00:08:03,160
What should I do?

144
00:08:03,160 --> 00:08:05,640
What do I do?

145
00:08:06,080 --> 00:08:06,600
I...

146
00:08:18,880 --> 00:08:19,560
What do I do?

147
00:08:19,560 --> 00:08:49,180
All right, pencils down.

148
00:08:49,560 --> 00:08:52,240
Hell yeah! We are free, my dudes!

149
00:08:53,340 --> 00:08:54,920
We're done!

150
00:08:58,180 --> 00:09:01,520
I should probably finish the apron and headdress first.

151
00:09:02,420 --> 00:09:04,620
Hey, Marion. How'd it go?

152
00:09:06,340 --> 00:09:07,500
Fine, I guess.

153
00:09:13,100 --> 00:09:14,140
He's weird.

154
00:09:16,560 --> 00:09:19,160
I figured he'd be home by this point.

155
00:09:20,300 --> 00:09:22,040
I guess I thought wrong.

156
00:09:23,080 --> 00:09:26,960
Maybe now that midterms are over, he can relax and be with his grandpa?

157
00:09:30,580 --> 00:09:32,940
Oh, Gojo. I hope he's okay.

158
00:09:32,940 --> 00:09:38,400
I guess it's a lonely dinner for one.

159
00:09:38,400 --> 00:09:55,920
My head hurts.

160
00:09:56,660 --> 00:09:57,680
I feel sick.

161
00:09:58,400 --> 00:09:59,660
Like I'm gonna throw up.

162
00:10:00,480 --> 00:10:02,000
I can't focus on anything.

163
00:10:03,700 --> 00:10:05,920
When was the last time I really slept?

164
00:10:05,920 --> 00:10:11,380
The outfit.

165
00:10:12,380 --> 00:10:13,980
It's not even close to being done.

166
00:10:14,840 --> 00:10:15,760
I've let her down.

167
00:10:16,760 --> 00:10:18,540
Kitagawa was so excited about it.

168
00:10:19,400 --> 00:10:20,880
She's gonna be heartbroken.

169
00:10:20,880 --> 00:10:26,140
My brushes.

170
00:10:26,560 --> 00:10:27,360
Could you bring them?

171
00:10:30,080 --> 00:10:32,240
Why are you bringing your brushes on the trip?

172
00:10:32,900 --> 00:10:33,200
Hmm?

173
00:10:33,780 --> 00:10:37,780
Well, I have to keep these hands moving, or they'll get rusty and won't work.

174
00:10:38,080 --> 00:10:42,620
If I skip even a day, it takes another three days to get the hang of it again.

175
00:10:42,620 --> 00:10:47,460
I don't even know how to use them properly yet.

176
00:10:48,180 --> 00:10:50,220
It's been so long since I've touched them.

177
00:10:51,660 --> 00:10:54,740
Maybe I'm not cut out for it after all.

178
00:10:54,740 --> 00:10:58,720
Just because you love to do something doesn't mean you do it well.

179
00:10:59,440 --> 00:11:03,120
You can work hard, but that doesn't mean it'll pay off.

180
00:11:04,620 --> 00:11:07,460
What am I gonna do with my life if I can't become a kashirashi?

181
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:13,240
What will Kitagawa say when she hears the outfit's not done?

182
00:11:14,180 --> 00:11:15,700
Why can't I do anything right?

183
00:11:16,280 --> 00:11:17,100
What a joke!

184
00:11:19,780 --> 00:11:21,880
I am such a pathetic failure.

185
00:11:21,880 --> 00:11:29,320
I'm just limping along, half-ashing my way through my entire life.

186
00:11:49,800 --> 00:11:50,720
Hey, Grandpa.

187
00:11:51,880 --> 00:11:52,120
Hmm?

188
00:11:53,080 --> 00:11:55,360
Isn't it hard making Hino dolls every day?

189
00:11:56,140 --> 00:11:57,080
Don't your hands hurt?

190
00:11:58,420 --> 00:12:00,300
Aren't you tired of working so much?

191
00:12:02,560 --> 00:12:03,700
Well, you're right.

192
00:12:03,760 --> 00:12:04,400
It is hard.

193
00:12:04,780 --> 00:12:06,940
Loving something doesn't make it easy to do.

194
00:12:08,420 --> 00:12:14,200
But then again, it's because you love working on it that you can stick it out when things get rough.

195
00:12:14,200 --> 00:12:21,440
Whenever I see our customers smile, I'm grateful I chose to do this, beautiful.

196
00:12:22,580 --> 00:12:22,980
Look.

197
00:12:26,180 --> 00:12:26,740
Whoa.

198
00:12:26,740 --> 00:12:34,740
When what you do makes someone happy, that makes you want to keep going, even if it's hard.

199
00:12:34,740 --> 00:12:44,060
Hey, Gojo.

200
00:12:45,200 --> 00:12:46,400
You're the best.

201
00:12:47,520 --> 00:12:48,960
It's fine not to compromise.

202
00:12:49,560 --> 00:12:51,800
I've got some things I'm pretty hardcore about, too.

203
00:12:52,800 --> 00:12:53,340
Hell yeah!

204
00:12:53,880 --> 00:12:56,340
Where's the first place I should wear it once it's complete?

205
00:12:56,880 --> 00:12:58,400
You saved me so much time.

206
00:12:58,560 --> 00:12:59,460
And money, too.

207
00:12:59,460 --> 00:13:01,380
Thank you.

208
00:13:01,380 --> 00:13:26,400
I need scissors.

209
00:13:27,120 --> 00:13:27,920
Where are they?

210
00:13:28,420 --> 00:13:29,520
Don't tell me they're missing.

211
00:13:29,520 --> 00:13:29,580
I need scissors.

212
00:13:31,380 --> 00:13:33,380
I need scissors.

213
00:14:01,380 --> 00:14:15,620
No way.

214
00:14:19,620 --> 00:14:23,720
It was a close call, but it's finished somehow, and you can go to your event.

215
00:14:23,720 --> 00:14:26,460
Hold on.

216
00:14:26,840 --> 00:14:27,760
What are you saying?

217
00:14:29,380 --> 00:14:31,940
You thought I wanted to cosplay at today's event?

218
00:14:32,600 --> 00:14:33,040
What?

219
00:14:33,240 --> 00:14:34,100
So you mean you're not?

220
00:14:37,140 --> 00:14:37,960
I mean, I...

221
00:14:38,540 --> 00:14:42,140
I had absolutely no idea how long it takes to make clothing.

222
00:14:42,840 --> 00:14:46,360
And there are actually quite a few cosplay events around if you search for them.

223
00:14:46,720 --> 00:14:51,100
Since I didn't know what our timeline was, I was just gonna wait until you were finished.

224
00:14:51,100 --> 00:14:55,480
I am so sorry.

225
00:14:55,480 --> 00:14:57,440
I didn't realize I wasn't clear.

226
00:14:57,680 --> 00:14:59,540
Now you're exhausted because of me.

227
00:15:01,220 --> 00:15:02,240
Oh, wow.

228
00:15:03,340 --> 00:15:04,820
That's such a relief.

229
00:15:04,820 --> 00:15:10,260
I was so anxious about not finishing, so I rushed through it.

230
00:15:11,080 --> 00:15:13,040
I'm thrilled there's still some time.

231
00:15:14,320 --> 00:15:15,680
Oh, thank goodness.

232
00:15:16,200 --> 00:15:16,760
For real.

233
00:15:16,760 --> 00:15:17,200
Oh.

234
00:15:19,200 --> 00:15:19,380
Huh?

235
00:15:19,380 --> 00:15:25,820
Wait, what'd I do?

236
00:15:26,440 --> 00:15:33,560
No, it's just that during exams, you said you went home to study, but I thought you were visiting your grandpa.

237
00:15:34,160 --> 00:15:35,420
I didn't know.

238
00:15:36,040 --> 00:15:37,060
I'm such an idiot.

239
00:15:37,820 --> 00:15:39,060
I should have realized.

240
00:15:39,060 --> 00:15:45,500
You've been dealing with so much, and somehow you still made time to finish the outfit.

241
00:15:46,880 --> 00:15:47,740
I'm sorry.

242
00:15:48,260 --> 00:15:48,920
I promise.

243
00:15:49,440 --> 00:15:51,940
I had no idea you were doing that for me.

244
00:15:53,380 --> 00:15:55,060
Please, forgive me.

245
00:15:55,600 --> 00:15:56,220
I'm sorry.

246
00:15:56,780 --> 00:15:57,840
I'm so sorry.

247
00:15:57,840 --> 00:16:10,620
Hey, so, uh, I'm sorry, too.

248
00:16:10,860 --> 00:16:12,440
I should have let you know what I was doing.

249
00:16:13,220 --> 00:16:14,900
That's why we exchanged numbers, right?

250
00:16:15,360 --> 00:16:17,520
This is all my fault for not being clear.

251
00:16:18,420 --> 00:16:19,440
No, it's not.

252
00:16:19,780 --> 00:16:20,680
I'm sorry.

253
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:22,040
I'm so sorry.

254
00:16:22,280 --> 00:16:22,680
Really.

255
00:16:22,840 --> 00:16:23,420
Come on.

256
00:16:23,800 --> 00:16:26,180
Hey, please, don't cry.

257
00:16:26,180 --> 00:16:33,000
So, um, why don't you try it on?

258
00:16:33,420 --> 00:16:34,660
Let's make sure it fits.

259
00:16:36,460 --> 00:16:40,520
Now that there's more time, I can tailor it properly and see if anything needs taking in.

260
00:16:41,440 --> 00:16:42,240
Oh, yeah.

261
00:16:42,700 --> 00:16:45,060
We should also see how everything looks all together.

262
00:16:45,540 --> 00:16:46,960
Put your wig on and makeup, too.

263
00:16:47,900 --> 00:16:48,340
What?

264
00:16:48,920 --> 00:16:50,480
You want me to do it right now?

265
00:16:50,880 --> 00:16:53,020
But you're totally exhausted, aren't you?

266
00:16:53,200 --> 00:16:53,940
Listen to me.

267
00:16:54,260 --> 00:16:54,560
Huh?

268
00:16:54,560 --> 00:16:56,300
